
# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Subject: imperative mood, lowercase, no full stop, <= 72 chars.
#   "add filled quantity to orders"   not   "Added filled quantity"
#
# type:  feat fix refactor perf test docs chore build ci
# scope: api wallet orders market orderbook db frontend infra
#
# ---- body: wrap at 72 -------------------------------------------------|
#
# Explain WHY, not HOW. The diff already shows how.
#   - What was wrong or missing before this change?
#   - What does this change make possible, or make impossible?
#   - What did you consider and reject, if it is not obvious?
#
# ---- before you save --------------------------------------------------
#
#  [ ] One logical change. If the subject needs "and", split the commit.
#  [ ] Tests for this change are in THIS commit, not a later one.
#  [ ] Builds, and tests pass.
#  [ ] Every line is one you can explain. If you cannot, cut it.
#  [ ] Nothing unrelated snuck in — check `git diff --cached` once more.
#
# Lines starting with # are stripped and will not appear in the message.
